Debian, Red Hat and others disable font ops by default, so we follow the
same approach to be better with security.

Ref: CVE-2022-45063 (34788211)

--- xterm-410/XTerm.ad
+++ xterm-410/XTerm.ad
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@ ! All of these features can be enabled o
 !
 ! Depending on your environment, you may wish to disable those by default by
 ! uncommenting one or more of the resource settings below:
-!*allowFontOps: false
+*allowFontOps: false
 !*allowTcapOps: false
 !*allowTitleOps: false
 !*allowWindowOps: false
